  "summary": "Alongside traditional arts and crafts, Zambia has a modern and contemporary visual art scene, with artists working in painting, printmaking, sculpture, photography and mixed media.",
  "description": "Visual arts: Alongside traditional arts and crafts, Zambia has a modern and contemporary visual art scene, with artists working in painting, printmaking, sculpture, photography and mixed media. The Lechwe Trust, founded in 1986, has played an important role in supporting visual arts in Zambia through grants, scholarships, exhibitions and the collecting of contemporary Zambian art.\n\nImportant figures in modern Zambian art include Henry Tayali, Flinto Chandia and Lutanda Mwamba. Chandia, who worked in wood, stone and metal, was a founder member of the Zambia National Visual Arts Council and was associated with artists' workshops including Mbile and Kabasa. Mwamba was known particularly for printmaking and painting. In 2019 the Lechwe Trust held Art Lives On – ii, a retrospective exhibition of work by Chandia and Mwamba, presenting sculptures, paintings and prints produced across several decades.",
  "culturalContext": "Compiled from the “Visual arts” section of Wikipedia's “Zambia”.",
